course: dictionary
lesson: 11531
title: Almsgiving: giving to people in need
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from religion, and the words around them give you the meaning. Look for clues. «Each Friday, the mosque gives food to families who have little.» Families who have little are poor, so giving them food is a kind of almsgiving.
explain: You can see the word giving inside almsgiving. It means giving money, food or help to people in need. «In Lent, Amira's church asks everyone to practise prayer, fasting and almsgiving.» Prayer and fasting are religious too, so the clues show that almsgiving is a religious duty.
explain: Almsgiving is not always money. «The class collected tins of food as their almsgiving for the food bank.» Food counts too. The sentence tells you that almsgiving is a way of helping people who need it. Try your meaning in the sentence: does giving food to people in need make sense? Yes, so you have it right.
fact: Almsgiving means giving money, food or help to poor people.
fact: Almsgiving is often a religious duty, which means believers give because their faith asks them to.
fact: Almsgiving is charity given out of kindness to people in need.
fact: In Lent, Christians often practise prayer, fasting and almsgiving.
fact: In Islam, giving to the poor, called zakat, is one of the Five Pillars.
exercise: «The family gave food to the homeless shelter as a form of almsgiving.» What does almsgiving mean? | Going on a long journey | Cooking a big dinner for the family | Singing in a church choir | *Giving money, food or help to people in need
exercise: Which of these is NOT one of the Lent practices in «prayer, fasting and almsgiving»? | *Shopping for sweets | Prayer | Almsgiving | Fasting
exercise: Why do many believers practise almsgiving? | To get on the news | *Because their faith asks them to help people in need | Because it is a school rule | To win a prize at school
test: Which word means giving money or food to poor people as a religious duty? | Fasting | *Almsgiving | Lent | Prayer
test: «Each week, the class collected tins of food for almsgiving.» What does this sentence show almsgiving means? | Learning to read a new book | *Helping people in need with food | Cleaning the classroom floor | Playing a game together
exam: Which of these best explains almsgiving in religion? | Buying new clothes for yourself | Reading a book quietly in the library | Winning a race at sports day | *Giving to the poor because your faith asks you to
